ot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "52f40ccd834aaab7ac53f555879411bf4897dc5b68d572af815dc32e7284b121" "basis" 1292 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162" "basis" 1292 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "a5112db55b664532de0130c202c6b6e919c5c44ac143c1b3e00ea18492050162" "basis" 1292 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a" "basis" 1292 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "7b0302819c882ad98b46d9e471117c6f55cf0debed9240f0e7ab4734d6d5219a" "basis" 1292 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037782/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-1091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the minor of the entry ${x}_{21}$ in the matrix\n$X=[\\begin{aligned}9 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 8 & 6 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-1091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 0 & 11\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${x}_{21}=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot 11-0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-33-0 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-1091" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-1091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-1091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-33"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "77"] ["math" "82"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-1091" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-33"] "category" "model_interpretatio