ned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the entry ${a}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =12-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319106" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319106" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{13}$ of the element ${f}_{13}.$\n\n${M}_{13}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{13},$ we remove the first row and third column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{13} & =det[\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-v\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-5v\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319125" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319125" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18-5v"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & 3 \\\\ y & 5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & x\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${p}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${p}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4y-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319164" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319164" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319164" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4y-x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the matrix\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}j & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & k & 5 \\\\ 4 & j & k\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{21}$ of the element ${v}_{21}.$\n\n${M}_{21}=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${v}_{21},$ we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & j & k\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${v}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{21} & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(3i)\\cdot j \\\\  & =k-3ij.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319176" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319176" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "k-3ij"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of ${t}_{22}$ in the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}3p & r & 3p \\\\ q & r & -q \\\\ -6q & -p & 6q\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and the second column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3p & ∗ & 3p \\\\ ∗ & r & ∗ \\\\ -6q & ∗ & 6q\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}3p & 3p \\\\ -6q & 6q\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}3p & 3p \\\\ -6q & 6q\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3p\\cdot 6q-3p\\cdot (-6q) \\\\  & =18pq+18pq \\\\  & =36pq\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-128024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answe