se_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319162" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319162" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14p-6q"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}t & -8 \\\\ -1 & 9\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =t\\cdot 9-(-8)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =9t-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is ${t}^{2}+12$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9t-8 & ={t}^{2}+12 \\\\ {t}^{2}-9t+20 & =0 \\\\ (t-5)(t-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $t=4$ and $t=5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$t=-4$ only"] ["text" "$t=-5$ and $t=-4$ only"] ["text" "$t=-5$ and $t=4$ only"] ["text" "$t=4$ and $t=5$ only"] ["text" "$t=5$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$t=4$ and $t=5$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-5t & 18 & 6t \\\\ -3 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 19t & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5t & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 9 & 5 \\\\ ∗ & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 3t-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =27t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27t-5 & =4 \\\\ 27t & =9 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=\\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "t=17"] ["math" "t=23"] ["math" "t=\\frac{19}{3}"] ["math" "t=\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "t=\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-128082" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "t=\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2k & -8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 11 & 9 & k+3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2k & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 11 & ∗ & k+3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${a}_{22}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}2k & 6 \\\\ 11 & k+3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2k\\cdot (k+3)-11\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+6k-66.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{22}$ is $-70$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+6k-66 & =-70 \\\\ 2{k}^{2}+6k+4 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2}+3k+2 & =0 \\\\ (k+1)(k+2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$k=-1$ and $k=-2$ only"] ["text" "$k=-2$ only"] ["text" "$k=0$ and $k=-1$ only"] ["text" "$k=1$ only"] ["text" "$k=10$ and $k=-3$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$k=-1$ and $k=-2$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, find all the possible values of $x$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & -10 \\\\ -5 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the third row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} & ∗ \\\\ -5 & 8 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${b}_{33}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -{x}^{2} \\\\ -5 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =6\\cdot 8-(-5)\\cdot (-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =48-5{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{33}$ is $3$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}48-5{x}^{2} & =3 \\\\ 45-5{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 9-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (3-x)(3+x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-3$ and $x=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only"] ["text" "$x=-9$ and $x=9$ only"] ["text" "$x=-9$ only"] ["text" "$x=6$ only"] ["text" "$x=9$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-18243" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-3$ and $x=3$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319138" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9452e3b6afc64d33d3bfab6d739e6e806217f9035d2200e6d8634a051ff57a07"} {"question" "q-319138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "q-319138" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{11}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/state.json" "file_sha256" "9dfc70a0a5535d42620d1b6447e4094ec1529a117c560001652cf3bb620ad693"} {"question" "e-4439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/8e664813c6467d5bb06a8eb1e1d68778d3142479939624a7a46674f593d786b9.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "f5850ea3be420e6c2c2a7357b66a6b8ea1abf82f1575457da8821464488e7f24"} {"question" "e-4439" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/a69955fcba387ef3c65f1c1529c2007d8d70f82d95738af9b995999a21198730.png)\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4439.json" "file_sha256" "f5850ea3be420e6c2c2a7357b66a6b8ea1abf82f1575457da8821464488e7f24"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/1449dfd139653f75de7be2e27e86f0c9d2d8a5a17e25ae184b892f489ffbb71e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "2e9ef04aa921b02654e895280f8ff2068f31f8fbb4d66e1eec21c56c3bfd12f7"} {"question" "e-4440" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/09bd73c7e51abcad8efa354317519a2687601b3ccdbfea0ac2b6222f75b3397e.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4440.json" "file_sha256" "2e9ef04aa921b02654e895280f8ff2068f31f8fbb4d66e1eec21c56c3bfd12f7"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/1d37ba9039f24a96be2d148c9f30c8a10ca30c9745ad8a28df23de5a42f6dcab.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "304c103d858d9e20e68045e4641348434dadee7967ba81d475efcd0a407e9fb3"} {"question" "e-4441" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/assets/80f9b95139f7b571c7752ee1feec4c9d3df8456223581736ae019344a6f9a080.png)\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14075201/example-4441.json" "file_sha256" "304c103d858d9e20e68045e4641348434dadee7967ba81d475efcd0a407e9fb3"}] "usage" {"q-127699" [] "e-4440" [] "q-69858" [] "q-18246" [] "e-4439" [] "q-1094" [] "q-128024" [] "e-4441" []} "basis" 2752 "retractions" [[17592186059909 :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry $y_{13}$ in the matrix\n\n$Y = \\begin{bmatrix}15 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186060063 :question/problem "Given that the minor of $p_{23}$ is $t^{2} + 12$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$P = \\begin{bmatrix}t & -8 & 3 \\\\ -7 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$."] [17592186059484 :question/problem "Calculate the minor of the entry $b_{21}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}10 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186059484 :question/worked-solution "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059485 :question/problem "What is the minor of $c_{22}$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & 0 & -3y \\\\ 1 & x+2y & 4 \\\\ -y & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186059485 :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and second column: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}7x & ∗ & -3y \\\\ ∗ & x+2y & ∗ \\\\ -y & ∗ & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}7x & -3y \\\\ -y & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =7x\\cdot 5-(-3y)\\cdot (-y) \\\\  & =35x-3{y}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186059486 :question/problem "Given that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ find all the possible values of $k$ in the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & -6\\end{aligned}]\n$$"] [17592186059486 :question/worked-solution "First, we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 7 \\\\ -1 & 2k & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of $a_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ -1 & 2k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =k\\cdot 2k-3\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2{k}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of $a_{23}$ is $5,$ so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{k}^{2}+3 & =5 \\\\ 2{k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =1 \\\\ k & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $k=-1$ and $k=1.$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186056174 17592186056175 17592186056176 17592186056177 17592186056178 17592186057106 17592186057107 17592186057108 17592186057109 17592186057110 17592186298265 17592186298266 17592186298267 17592186298268 17592186298269 17592186298285 17592186298286 17592186298287 17592186298288 17592186298289 17592186298320 17592186298321 17592186298322 17592186298323 17592186298324] "immutable_fields" [[17592186056173 :answer-field/correct] [17592186